{"id":"o1-02-p2","title":"Processes and threads","scopeHtml":"<p>Scope: process vs program, PCB and states, fork/exec, copy-on-write, threads and thread models, context switch cost. Questions are still to be written.</p>","notes":[{"id":"process-vs-program","title":"Process vs program","html":"<p><strong>A program is a file on disk (instructions). A process is a program that is running, with its own memory, open files and state.</strong> Run the same program twice and you get two processes.</p>\n<p>A process owns:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>A private <strong>virtual address space</strong>: code, data, heap, stack, mapped libraries.</li>\n<li><strong>Open file descriptors</strong> (0 stdin, 1 stdout, 2 stderr, then sockets, files).</li>\n<li><strong>Credentials</strong> (user ID, group ID), current directory, environment variables, signal handlers.</li>\n<li>One or more <strong>threads</strong> of execution.</li>\n</ul>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 309.2 192\" width=\"309.2\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"One process, many resources\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M102 96 L158 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"1.6s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 96 L158 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"1.6s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M102 96 L158 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"1.6s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 96 L158 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"1.6s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M102 96 L158 158\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"1.6s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 96 L158 158\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"1.6s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"74\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"57\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Process</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"12\" width=\"139.2\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"227.6\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Address space</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"74\" width=\"139.2\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"227.6\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">File descriptors</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"136\" width=\"139.2\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"227.6\" y=\"162\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Threads</text></svg><figcaption>One process, many resources</figcaption></figure>\n<p>You can see it all in <code>/proc</code>:</p>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span>$ ls /proc/$$           # $$ = this shell</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>cmdline  cwd  environ  exe  fd  maps  smaps  stat  status  task ...</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>$ grep -E 'Name|State|Pid|PPid|Threads|VmRSS' /proc/$$/status</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>Name:   bash</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>State:  S (sleeping)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>Pid:    3120</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>PPid:   3101</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>VmRSS:  4120 kB</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>Threads:        1</span></span></code></pre>\n<p><strong>Worked example.</strong> A Postgres server forks one backend process per client connection, each about 5 to 10 MB of private memory. 500 connections cost 2.5 to 5 GB before any query runs, which is why PgBouncer pooling is standard past a few hundred connections.</p>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> Chrome runs one process per tab for isolation (a crash or exploit stays inside it). Nginx uses a few worker processes, each handling thousands of connections with epoll. Postgres is process-per-connection; MySQL is thread-per-connection.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> A recipe (program) versus a cook actually cooking it in their own kitchen (process). Two cooks on one recipe are two processes.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Using \"process\" and \"program\" as synonyms.</li>\n<li>Forgetting that the isolation boundary is the process: one process cannot read another's memory without OS help.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"process-states-and-the-pcb","title":"Process states and the PCB","html":"<p><strong>The kernel tracks each process in a record called the Process Control Block (PCB).</strong> In Linux it is <code>struct task_struct</code> (a few KB). It holds: PID, state, saved CPU registers, page table pointer, open files table, signal state, scheduling info (priority, vruntime), parent and children, cgroup and namespace links.</p>\n<p><strong>States</strong> (what <code>ps</code> and <code>top</code> show in the <code>S</code> column):</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>R</code> running or runnable (on a CPU or in the run queue)</li>\n<li><code>S</code> sleeping, interruptible (waiting for an event; can take signals)</li>\n<li><code>D</code> uninterruptible sleep (usually waiting on disk or NFS; cannot be killed)</li>\n<li><code>T</code> stopped (Ctrl-Z or debugger)</li>\n<li><code>Z</code> zombie (finished, parent has not collected exit code)</li>\n</ul>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 844 130\" width=\"844\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Life of a process\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M102 65 L596 65\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 65 L596 65\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.167;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.167;0.168;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M686 65 L742 65\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M686 65 L742 65\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.667;0.833;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.667;0.833;0.834;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M540 34 L596 65\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M540 34 L596 65\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"43\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"57\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">New</text><rect x=\"450\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"495\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Sleeping</text><rect x=\"450\" y=\"74\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"495\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Zombie</text><rect x=\"596\" y=\"43\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"641\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Runnable</text><rect x=\"742\" y=\"43\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"787\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Running</text></svg><figcaption>Life of a process</figcaption></figure>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span>$ ps -eo pid,ppid,stat,wchan:20,cmd | head</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>  PID  PPID STAT WCHAN                CMD</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>    1     0 Ss   do_epoll_wait        /sbin/init</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span> 2210  2188 D    io_schedule          dd if=/dev/sda of=/dev/null</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span> 2301  1200 Z    -                    [worker] &#x3C;defunct></span></span></code></pre>\n<p><strong>Production incident patterns.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Many <code>D</code> processes and a load average of 50 on an idle CPU: storage or NFS hang. <code>wchan</code> shows where; fix the disk, a <code>kill -9</code> will not help.</li>\n<li>A growing pile of <code>Z</code> zombies: the parent never calls <code>wait()</code>. Each costs a PID and a PCB, not memory; at the PID limit (<code>/proc/sys/kernel/pid_max</code>, often 32768 or 4M) <code>fork</code> fails with <code>EAGAIN</code>. Fix the parent, or kill it so <code>init</code> adopts and reaps the zombies. In Docker, running an app as PID 1 that does not reap children causes this; use <code>--init</code> or <code>tini</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> A hospital patient chart: name, status, medication, where the patient is. The doctors (CPU) pick up charts, not patients.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Thinking a zombie uses CPU or can be killed by <code>kill -9</code> (it is already dead; only the parent reaping removes it).</li>\n<li>Confusing <code>D</code> with <code>S</code>: <code>D</code> ignores signals and counts in load average.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"fork-and-exec","title":"fork and exec","html":"<p><strong>Unix creates processes in two steps: <code>fork()</code> clones the current process, <code>exec()</code> replaces the clone's program with a new one.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>fork()</code> returns twice: the child gets 0, the parent gets the child's PID. Child has a copy of memory, same open files, same environment.</li>\n<li><code>execve(path, argv, envp)</code> throws away the address space and loads a new program; PID stays the same, file descriptors stay open unless marked close-on-exec.</li>\n<li><code>wait()/waitpid()</code> lets the parent collect the exit status.</li>\n</ul>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">import</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> os</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">pid </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">=</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> os.fork()</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">if</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> pid </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">==</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> 0</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">:                      </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D\"># child</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">    os.execvp(</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"ls\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">, [</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"ls\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">, </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"-l\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">])  </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D\"># becomes ls</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">else</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">:                              </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D\"># parent</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">    os.waitpid(pid, </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">0</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">)             </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D\"># reap, avoids zombie</span></span></code></pre>\n<p>Why two steps? The gap lets a shell set up redirection between them: after <code>fork</code>, the child does <code>dup2(fd, 1)</code> to point stdout at a file, then <code>exec</code>s the command. That is how <code>ls > out.txt</code> and pipes work.</p>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 565.2 130\" width=\"565.2\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"How a shell runs a command\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M102 65 L158 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 65 L158 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;0.251;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M248 34 L304 65\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M248 34 L304 65\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M407.2 65 L463.2 65\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M407.2 65 L463.2 65\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;0.751;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M102 65 L158 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 65 L158 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;0.251;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"43\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"57\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Shell</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"203\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">fork</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"74\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"203\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">wait</text><rect x=\"304\" y=\"43\" width=\"103.2\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"355.6\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Child shell</text><rect x=\"463.2\" y=\"43\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"508.2\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">exec ls</text></svg><figcaption>How a shell runs a command</figcaption></figure>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span>$ strace -f -e trace=clone,execve,wait4 sh -c 'ls >/dev/null'</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>clone(child_stack=NULL, flags=CLONE_CHILD_CLEARTID|SIGCHLD) = 4201</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>[pid 4201] execve(\"/bin/ls\", [\"ls\"], ...) = 0</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>wait4(-1, [{WIFEXITED(s) &#x26;&#x26; WEXITSTATUS(s) == 0}], 0, NULL) = 4201</span></span></code></pre>\n<p>Modern libc <code>fork</code> is really the <code>clone</code> syscall. For spawning, <code>posix_spawn</code> and <code>vfork</code> avoid copying page tables; <code>vfork</code> suspends the parent until the child execs.</p>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> Redis <code>BGSAVE</code> forks, and the child writes the snapshot while the parent keeps serving. Android's Zygote preloads the framework once and forks for every app, so app start shares already-loaded classes.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> Photocopy a form (fork), then white-out it and write a completely different one (exec).</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Believing fork copies all memory immediately (see next section).</li>\n<li>Forking a huge multithreaded process: only the calling thread survives in the child, other threads' locks may stay locked forever. Prefer <code>posix_spawn</code> or exec right away.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"copy-on-write","title":"Copy-on-write","html":"<p><strong>After <code>fork</code>, parent and child share the same physical pages, marked read-only. Only when one of them writes does the kernel copy that single page.</strong> This makes fork fast even for gigabytes of memory.</p>\n<p>Mechanism: fork copies the page tables (not the data) and marks every writable page read-only in both. A write triggers a page fault; the fault handler sees \"COW page\", allocates a new frame, copies 4 KB, maps it writable for the writer, and resumes.</p>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 1016 68\" width=\"1016\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"First write after fork copies one page\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M230.4 34 L286.4 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M230.4 34 L286.4 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.200;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.200;0.201;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M396.79999999999995 34 L452.79999999999995 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M396.79999999999995 34 L452.79999999999995 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.200;0.400;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.200;0.400;0.401;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M548.8 34 L604.8 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M548.8 34 L604.8 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.400;0.600;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.400;0.600;0.601;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M758.4 34 L814.4 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M758.4 34 L814.4 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.600;0.800;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.600;0.800;0.801;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"12\" width=\"218.4\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"121.2\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Parent and child share page</text><rect x=\"286.4\" y=\"12\" width=\"110.4\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"341.59999999999997\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Child writes</text><rect x=\"452.79999999999995\" y=\"12\" width=\"96\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"500.79999999999995\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Page fault</text><rect x=\"604.8\" y=\"12\" width=\"153.6\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"681.5999999999999\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Kernel copies 4 KB</text><rect x=\"814.4\" y=\"12\" width=\"189.6\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"909.1999999999999\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Child gets private page</text></svg><figcaption>First write after fork copies one page</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Worked example.</strong> Redis with 20 GB of data forks for a snapshot. Fork itself copies about 40 MB of page tables (20 GB / 4 KB pages x 8 bytes) and takes tens of ms (longer in VMs; Redis exposes <code>latest_fork_usec</code>). If the parent then updates 10% of pages during the 60 s snapshot, about 2 GB of extra RAM is needed. Machines with only 22 GB RAM would be OOM-killed. Rule of thumb: leave headroom, or set <code>vm.overcommit_memory=1</code> as Redis docs advise so fork is not refused.</p>\n<p><strong>Transparent Huge Pages hurt here:</strong> one write copies 2 MB instead of 4 KB, causing latency spikes and RAM blow-up; Redis recommends disabling THP.</p>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D\"># Is memory shared? Look at Shared_Clean/Private_Dirty per mapping</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">grep</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> -E</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> 'Rss|Pss|Private_Dirty'</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> /proc/</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">&#x3C;</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">pi</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">d</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">></span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">/smaps_rollup</span></span></code></pre>\n<p>PSS (proportional set size) splits shared pages fairly among sharers: the honest per-process memory figure.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> Two students share one textbook. The moment one wants to scribble in it, they photocopy only that page for themselves.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Answering \"fork duplicates memory\": the correct answer is page tables plus COW.</li>\n<li>Forgetting COW is also why <code>exec</code> right after <code>fork</code> is cheap: nothing was copied.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"threads","title":"Threads","html":"<p><strong>A thread is a unit of execution inside a process. Threads of one process share the address space and file descriptors but each has its own stack, registers and program counter.</strong></p>\n<p>Shared: heap, globals, code, open files. Private: stack (default 8 MB virtual on Linux main thread; Java threads default to about 1 MB), registers, thread-local storage, signal mask.</p>\n<p>In Linux a thread is just a task created with <code>clone(CLONE_VM | CLONE_FILES | CLONE_FS | CLONE_SIGHAND | CLONE_THREAD...)</code>; the kernel schedules threads, not processes. <code>ps -L</code>, <code>top -H</code> and <code>/proc/&#x3C;pid>/task/</code> list them.</p>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 419.2 192\" width=\"419.2\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"One process, three threads sharing memory\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M102 96 L158 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 96 L158 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M102 96 L158 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 96 L158 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M102 96 L158 158\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 96 L158 158\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M248 34 L304 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M248 34 L304 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M248 96 L304 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M248 96 L304 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M248 158 L304 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M248 158 L304 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"74\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"57\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Process</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"203\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Thread 1</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"74\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"203\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Thread 2</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"136\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"203\" y=\"162\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Thread 3</text><rect x=\"304\" y=\"74\" width=\"103.2\" height=\"44\" rx=\"22\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"355.6\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Shared heap</text></svg><figcaption>One process, three threads sharing memory</figcaption></figure>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th></th>\n<th>Process</th>\n<th>Thread</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Memory</td>\n<td>Private</td>\n<td>Shared with siblings</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Creation cost</td>\n<td>Higher (page tables)</td>\n<td>Lower (about 10 to 50 microseconds)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Communication</td>\n<td>IPC needed</td>\n<td>Direct memory (with locks)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Crash</td>\n<td>Isolated</td>\n<td>Takes down the whole process</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><strong>Decision gravity.</strong> Threads are fast to talk to each other but any bug (data race, segfault) hits every thread. Processes isolate failures at the cost of IPC. Chosen per component; process-to-thread migration of a codebase is a large, hard-to-reverse rewrite.</p>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> Tomcat/Spring use a thread pool (default 200 threads). Node.js runs JS on one thread plus a libuv worker pool of 4. Go multiplexes goroutines (2 KB starting stacks) over few OS threads.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> Workers in one kitchen sharing the same fridge. Faster to hand things over, but one person dropping the pan hurts everyone.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Saying threads are \"lightweight processes\" without mentioning shared address space.</li>\n<li>Forgetting that one thread's uncaught segfault kills the whole process.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"thread-models","title":"Thread models","html":"<p><strong>How user-level threads map to kernel threads decides cost and parallelism.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>1:1 (kernel threads):</strong> every language thread is an OS thread. Used by Linux pthreads, Java platform threads, Rust <code>std::thread</code>. True parallelism, kernel schedules everything. Cost: memory per thread (stack plus kernel structures, roughly 1 to 2 MB virtual, less resident) and context switch cost; a few thousand threads is the practical limit.</li>\n<li><strong>N:1 (green threads):</strong> many user threads on one OS thread. Cheap, but no multicore and one blocking syscall stalls all. Old Java \"green threads\", early Ruby.</li>\n<li><strong>M:N (hybrid):</strong> many user-level tasks scheduled onto a small pool of OS threads. Go goroutines, Erlang processes (WhatsApp: millions per node), Java 21 virtual threads, Kotlin coroutines.</li>\n</ul>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 438.4 192\" width=\"438.4\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"M:N: many cheap tasks over few OS threads\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M115.2 34 L171.2 65\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M115.2 34 L171.2 65\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M274.4 65 L330.4 65\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M274.4 65 L330.4 65\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M115.2 96 L171.2 65\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M115.2 96 L171.2 65\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M115.2 158 L171.2 127\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M115.2 158 L171.2 127\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M274.4 127 L330.4 127\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M274.4 127 L330.4 127\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"12\" width=\"103.2\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"63.6\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Goroutine 1</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"74\" width=\"103.2\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"63.6\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Goroutine 2</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"136\" width=\"103.2\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"63.6\" y=\"162\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Goroutine 3</text><rect x=\"171.2\" y=\"43\" width=\"103.2\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"222.79999999999998\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">OS thread A</text><rect x=\"171.2\" y=\"105\" width=\"103.2\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"222.79999999999998\" y=\"131\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">OS thread B</text><rect x=\"330.4\" y=\"43\" width=\"96\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"378.4\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">CPU core 1</text><rect x=\"330.4\" y=\"105\" width=\"96\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"378.4\" y=\"131\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">CPU core 2</text></svg><figcaption>M:N: many cheap tasks over few OS threads</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Worked example.</strong> A server with 10,000 concurrent connections: thread-per-connection with 1 MB stacks is 10 GB virtual and heavy scheduler load. With an event loop (epoll plus a handful of threads) or virtual threads it is a few hundred MB. That is the C10K problem and why Nginx, Netty and Go replaced thread-per-request in high-connection servers.</p>\n<p><strong>Android link.</strong> Main (UI) thread must never block; blocking work goes to a pool or coroutine dispatcher (<code>Dispatchers.IO</code> is a pool of up to 64 threads by default). Coroutines are M:N in spirit.</p>\n<p><strong>Production signs.</strong> Thread leak: <code>Threads:</code> in <code>/proc/&#x3C;pid>/status</code> or <code>ps -o nlwp</code> grows until <code>pthread_create</code> fails with <code>EAGAIN</code> (\"unable to create new native thread\" in Java). Check <code>ulimit -u</code>, <code>/proc/sys/kernel/threads-max</code>, cgroup <code>pids.max</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> Waiters (OS threads) each serving many tables (tasks), instead of hiring one waiter per table.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Saying Go uses green threads on one core. It is M:N across all cores (<code>GOMAXPROCS</code>).</li>\n<li>Forgetting that a blocking call on an M:N runtime may pin an OS thread.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"context-switch-cost","title":"Context switch cost","html":"<p><strong>A context switch is the CPU stopping one thread and starting another.</strong> Steps: save registers of the old task into its PCB, pick the next task, load its registers, switch the page table (if different process), resume.</p>\n<p><strong>Direct cost</strong> is roughly 1 to 5 microseconds (kernel work, register save). <strong>Indirect cost</strong> is often bigger: the new task finds cold CPU caches and, after a process switch, a flushed or partly invalid TLB (PCID helps). Thread switch inside one process is cheaper as the address space stays the same.</p>\n<p>Types: <strong>voluntary</strong> (task blocked on I/O or a lock) and <strong>involuntary</strong> (its time slice ended or a higher priority task woke).</p>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D\"># Per-task counters</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">grep</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> ctxt</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> /proc/</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">&#x3C;</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">pi</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">d</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">></span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">/status</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">voluntary_ctxt_switches:</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">    81234</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">nonvoluntary_ctxt_switches:</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> 1520</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">pidstat</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> -w</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> 1</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D\">       # cswch/s (voluntary), nvcswch/s (involuntary)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">vmstat</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> 1</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D\">           # 'cs' column = system-wide switches/s</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">perf</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> stat</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> -e</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> context-switches,cpu-migrations</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> ./app</span></span></code></pre>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span>$ pidstat -w 1</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>11:20:01  UID  PID   cswch/s nvcswch/s  Command</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>11:20:02  1000 4410  12000.00    35.00  java</span></span></code></pre>\n<p>Reading: high voluntary rate means lots of blocking (locks, small I/O, chatty RPC). High involuntary rate with a long run queue (<code>r</code> in vmstat larger than cores) means CPU oversubscription: too many runnable threads.</p>\n<p><strong>Worked example.</strong> 20,000 switches/s per core x 5 microseconds = 10% of one core gone, plus cache misses. A thread pool of 2,000 threads on 8 cores spending time in lock handoff is a classic cause of high <code>sy</code> and low throughput; cutting to about 16 to 32 threads (CPU-bound) often raises throughput. For I/O-bound work size is roughly cores x (1 + wait/compute).</p>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 720 68\" width=\"720\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Many runnable threads causes switches and cold caches\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M151.2 34 L207.2 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M151.2 34 L207.2 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;0.251;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M353.6 34 L409.6 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M353.6 34 L409.6 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M512.8000000000001 34 L568.8000000000001 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M512.8000000000001 34 L568.8000000000001 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;0.751;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"12\" width=\"139.2\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"81.6\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Too many threads</text><rect x=\"207.2\" y=\"12\" width=\"146.4\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"280.4\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Frequent switches</text><rect x=\"409.6\" y=\"12\" width=\"103.2\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"461.20000000000005\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Cold caches</text><rect x=\"568.8000000000001\" y=\"12\" width=\"139.2\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"638.4000000000001\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Lower throughput</text></svg><figcaption>Many runnable threads causes switches and cold caches</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> LMAX Disruptor and Seastar (ScyllaDB) pin one thread per core and avoid locks to eliminate switching; Nginx uses one worker per core.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> Putting down one jigsaw and starting another: time lost saving your place and re-finding pieces, worse each time the table is cluttered.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Quoting a single number as fact. Say it depends on CPU and kernel, and name how to measure (<code>perf</code>, <code>pidstat -w</code>).</li>\n<li>Ignoring the indirect cache and TLB cost.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"summary","title":"Summary","html":"<ul>\n<li>Process = running program with private address space, file descriptors and credentials; the PCB (<code>task_struct</code>) tracks it.</li>\n<li>States R, S, D, T, Z; many <code>D</code> points to storage, many <code>Z</code> to a parent that does not <code>wait()</code>.</li>\n<li><code>fork</code> clones, <code>exec</code> replaces; the gap enables redirection and pipes. Prefer <code>posix_spawn</code> from big multithreaded parents.</li>\n<li>Copy-on-write makes fork cheap; Redis BGSAVE shows the memory spike when parents keep writing, and THP makes it worse.</li>\n<li>Threads share memory and fds, have private stacks; Linux threads are <code>clone</code> tasks seen with <code>top -H</code>.</li>\n<li>Models: 1:1, N:1, M:N; high connection counts favour event loops or M:N runtimes.</li>\n<li>Context switch costs 1 to 5 microseconds directly, more through cold caches; measure with <code>pidstat -w</code>, <code>vmstat cs</code>, size pools to cores.</li>\n</ul>"}],"questions":[]}